# variance.fw — variance Var[X] = E[(X - mean)^2] as a Sigma sum.
#
# The variance of a discrete random variable is the expected squared deviation
# from the mean:
#
#   Var[X] = sum over outcomes of  (value - mean)^2 * probability
#
# This file gives the discrete-UNIFORM case over {1..N} (probability 1/N each).
# The mean is itself a bounded aggregation (the same Sigma value*prob form as
# expected_value.fw), computed first into `mean`, then the squared-deviation sum
# folds against it:
#
#   variance(N) = sum((v - mean)^2 * (1/N), v in [1..N])
#
# For a fair 6-sided die: variance(6) = 35/12 ~ 2.9167.
# (Equivalent E[X^2] - mean^2 form folds to the same value; the deviation form
# is used here so every intermediate stays a clean Sigma over the domain.)
#
# Iterator named v, NOT i (imaginary unit) — see expected_value.fw.
#
# Usage:
#   variance(N=6, result=?s2)               # variance of a fair 6-sided die

[variance(N) -> result]
mean = sum(v * (1/N), v in [1..N])
result = sum((v - mean)^2 * (1/N), v in [1..N])
